{
 "text": "Two computers. One desk. A Mac... and a PC.\n\nAnd one email address you type twenty times a day. Letter... by letter.\n\n[sighs] So you keep it in a note, and copy it from there. Type it again... one letter wrong. And on a new computer? You start all over.\n\nWhat if one key could just... type it for you? On every computer?\n\nThis is KeyBridge.\n\nRight Shift and E... there it is. Left Shift and E? Still just a capital E. Left and right are different keys.\n\nOn your Mac, sign in and type your code once. Every shortcut is there. The only rule: sign in on each computer.\n\nType a short word for your whole signature. Open a link, a folder or a program with one key. And nothing you delete is ever lost.\n\nYour shortcuts are locked with a code only you have, before they leave your computer, so nobody else can read them. And KeyBridge never records what you type.\n\nIn English, Hebrew, Spanish, French, Russian, or Arabic.\n\nSo stop typing the same things over and over. Just press it... once.\n\nKeyBridge. Free and open source, for Mac and Windows.",
